# Ignore everything under data/ except the files that belong in git.
#
# These rules live HERE, not in the root .gitignore. A `/data/*` pattern in the root
# file makes DVC read `data/` itself as ignored: its ignore check tests directories
# with a trailing slash, and `*` matches the empty string, so `data/` matches. DVC then
# never walks into data/, finds no .dvc file, collects zero stages and reports
# "Everything is up to date" on pull without ever contacting the remote. Git disagrees
# with DVC here, so `git check-ignore` shows nothing wrong.
*
!.gitignore
!*.dvc
!README.md
# Month -> open data platform file ID, 1996.01-2026.07. Generated from the formula in
# download_monthly_packages.py, needed before any download: keep it in git.
!id_mapping.json
# Human labels cannot be regenerated: keep them in git (JIDs and short notes, no names)
!labels/
